insert into public.problems (id, title, source, url, difficulty_rating, statement_md, input_format_md, output_format_md, constraints_text, sample_io, target_complexity) values ('sbc-2025-final-c-clean-streets', 'Clean Streets', 'SBC Maratona', 'https://scorelatam.naquadah.com.br/latam-2025/contest.pdf', 1600, 'Problem C – Clean Streets
                                      Author : Roberto Sales, Brasil

One more year of Virada Cultural in São Paulo. The city is full of people, and the streets are full of
life. People from all over the city go to the streets to enjoy a night of cultural events and a lot of music.
Oswaldo, an employee at the city hall, was assigned the task of hiring cleaners to clean the S streets of
São Paulo, in no more than K hours after this big event. He was given by his boss a list of N cleaners
he could hire, numbered from 1 to N , along with information related to how fast they work and the
payment they accept. According to the list, cleaner i can clean any street in Hi hours, and accepts as
payment anything between Li and Ui for cleaning each street.
Oswaldo must hire a subset C of the cleaners that are in the list. For each hired cleaner i ∈ C he
must assign si streets for them to clean and a payment pi per street, taking into account the following
guidelines:

    • Each number of streets si must be a positive integer and the sum i∈C si must be exactly S,
                                                                           P
      because every street must be cleaned and no street can be cleaned by more than one cleaner.
    • Note that each hired cleaner i will take si · Hi hours to clean their assigned streets. Since the
      cleaners can work in parallel, the cleaning job will take, in total, maxi∈C (si · Hi ) hours to be
      completed. This total time must be at most K hours.
    • The payment per street pi must be a rational number between Li and Ui (that is, Li ≤ pi ≤ Ui ).
    • To ensure a fair hiring process, the payment per hour of work H
                                                                    pi
                                                                      i
                                                                        must be the same for all hired
      cleaners.

Notice that the above restrictions do not apply to the cleaners that are not hired.
                                                                           P
Hired cleaner i will receive si · pi as payment, being the total payment i∈C si · pi . Help Oswaldo
determine the minimum total payment for cleaning the streets honoring the given guidelines, or tell him
that those requirements cannot be satisfied.

Input
The first line contains three integers N , S and K (1 ≤ N, S ≤ 105 and 1 ≤ K ≤ 109 ), indicating
respectively the number of available cleaners, the number of streets to be cleaned, and in how many
hours the job must be completed. Each cleaner is identified by a distinct integer from 1 to N .
The i-th of the next N lines describes cleaner i with three integers Hi (1 ≤ Hi ≤ 105 ), Li and Ui
(1 ≤ Li ≤ Ui ≤ 100), indicating that the cleaner can clean any street in Hi hours, and accepts as
payment any value in the range [Li , Ui ].

Output
If the given guidelines can be satisfied, output a single line with two positive integers x and y, such that
x
y is an irreducible fraction indicating the minimum total payment for cleaning the streets according to
those guidelines.
If the requirements cannot be fulfilled, output a line with the character “*” (asterisk) instead.

 Sample input 1                                         Sample output 1
 2 15 10                                                80 1
 1 4 10
 2 2 8

 Sample input 2                                         Sample output 2
 2 7 9                                                  68 3
 3 4 10
 2 2 8

ICPC 

 Sample input 3                                     Sample output 3
 2 15 10                                            *
 1 4 10
 5 2 8

